cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use xlgit in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "xlgit: cell-level diff and merge for Excel workbooks in git"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fowler
    given-names: Michael
repository-code: "https://github.com/MichaelFowler1/excel-git"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  xlgit makes Excel workbooks work like code in git and GitHub. It diffs
  workbooks cell by cell and merges branches automatically, keeping charts,
  images, comments, tables, pivot tables and macros intact, and flags only
  the cells and objects both sides changed.
keywords:
  - excel
  - git
  - merge
  - diff
  - spreadsheets
  - version control
